<ehcache xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="../config/ehcache.xsd">

	<!--
	  L1 is the in-memory tier. A page fragment lands here only when it asks to, with
	  x-frontcache-component-cache-level: L1; everything else goes to L2 (the Lucene index).

	  overflowToDisk is OFF, and that is the important part of this file.

	  It used to be on, with diskStore path="/tmp". An entry evicted from memory was then
	  JAVA-SERIALIZED into Ehcache's own disk store: a second, slower, differently-formatted
	  on-disk cache sitting underneath an L2 Lucene index whose entire job is to be the disk
	  tier. Combined with eternal="true" and no maxElementsOnDisk, that store grew without
	  bound, in /tmp, which on many hosts is a tmpfs (so it was really RAM) and on all of them
	  is subject to being cleaned out from under the process. It also made purge() expensive:
	  scanning L1 for expired entries faulted every overflowed entry back off disk to read it.

	  Now an entry that does not fit is simply evicted. L2 still has it, or the origin does.

	  On sizing: maxElementsInMemory is a COUNT, and page fragments vary in size by orders of
	  magnitude, so a count cannot strictly bound heap. Ehcache's byte based sizing
	  (maxBytesLocalHeap) would, but it is NOT USABLE on this runtime: its SizeOf engine walks
	  the object graph by reflection and fails on Java 17+ with
	  "InaccessibleObjectException: module java.base does not open java.util", which could only
	  be worked around by adding an add-opens flag to every deployment's JVM arguments.

	  So: a count, raised from 100 (small enough that any site with more than a hundred
	  L1-marked fragments thrashed) to 1000, plus an explicit way to check the real number.
	  Frontcache tracks L1's actual content bytes itself (see L1ByteCounter) and exports it as
	  frontcache_cache_content_bytes{tier="L1"}. Watch that gauge and set this count to suit the
	  fragment sizes the site actually caches.
	-->
	<cache name="FRONT_CACHE"
	   maxElementsInMemory="1000"
	   eternal="true"
	   overflowToDisk="false"
	   memoryStoreEvictionPolicy="LFU"
	    />

</ehcache>
